# The committed synthetic test corpus under data/ (generated by
# `cargo run -p xtask`) depends on files being byte-identical - or
# identical-plus-one-line - across machines: that's how the exact and
# near-duplicate detection tests work. Without this, Windows's
# core.autocrlf would check out CRLF for text fixtures while Linux/macOS
# check out LF for the same commit, and git could misdetect the zip-based
# docx/pptx/xlsx fixtures as text and corrupt them. Force LF for text
# fixtures and explicit binary handling for the rest, so every OS in CI
# sees identical bytes.

data/** text=auto eol=lf

data/**/*.docx binary
data/**/*.pptx binary
data/**/*.xlsx binary
data/**/*.pdf binary
data/**/*.png binary
data/**/*.jpg binary
data/**/*.jpeg binary
data/**/*.gif binary
data/**/*.bmp binary
data/**/*.tiff binary
data/**/*.msg binary
